    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "mempool: keep prioritisetransaction deltas within MAX_MONEY",
    "user": {
      "login": "Bruce039",
      "id": 109469941,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBoZg9Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109469941?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bruce039",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`prioritisetransaction` takes `fee_delta` as any int64. `CTxMemPool::PrioritiseTransaction` stacks deltas with `SaturatingAdd`, so the accumulated delta and the modified fee can go up to `INT64_MAX`. The cluster mempool then adds modified fees of several transactions together in `FeeFrac` (util/feefrac.h:108) without overflow checks.\n\nFor example, with a parent and child in the mempool:\n\n```\nprioritisetransaction <parent> 0 4611686018427387904\nprioritisetransaction <child> 0 9223372036854775807\n```\n\n- `getmempoolcluster` reports `chunkfee: -46116860184.27356705`\n- `getblocktemplate` contains neither transaction, and the next block mined has only the coinbase\n- UBSan: `feefrac.h:108:13: runtime error: signed integer overflow`, reached from linearization via `getrawmempool`\n\nThere's no use for a delta larger than the total money supply, so this:\n\n- rejects `fee_delta` outside `-MAX_MONEY..MAX_MONEY` in the RPC with \"fee_delta out of range\"\n- clamps the accumulated delta to `-MAX_MONEY..MAX_MONEY` in `PrioritiseTransaction`, which also covers deltas loaded from mempool.dat, and updates the modified fee by the change in the clamped delta\n\nWith each modified fee bounded by 2 * MAX_MONEY, cluster sums stay far away from int64 limits.\n\nThe new `test_fee_delta_limits` in `mining_prioritisetransaction.py` checks the RPC range error, that stacked deltas stop at `MAX_MONEY`, that the chunk fees add up, and that both transactions are in the block template. It fails on master (\"No exception raised\"). `mempool_persist.py`, `mempool_packages.py`, `rpc_packages.py` and the miner/rbf/txpackage unit tests pass.\n\nAI tools were used to help find this issue and to prepare the patch and test.\n",
